The following uses of conditions shall be and are hereby prohibited within wellhead protection zones, whether or not such use or condition may otherwise be ordinarily included as a part of a use permitted under section 50-128 of this article:
(a) Surface use or storage of hazardous material, expressly including commercial use of agricultural pesticides;
(b) Septic tanks or drain fields appurtenant thereto;
(c) Impervious surfaces other than roofs of buildings and street and driveways and walks serving buildings permitted under section 50-128 of the article;
(d) Sanitary landfills;
(e) Hazardous waste disposal sites;
(f) Stormwater infiltration basins;
(g) Underground storage tanks;
(h) Sanitary sewer lines within 150 feet of a wellhead.
(Ord. No. 10,2004, § 5, 9-13-04)
